From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Adam <i@noc.cat>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 09:10:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 69/70] ACPI: utils: return early from acpi_evaluate_dsm()
 without a handle

Drivers for devices that exist on both ACPI and device tree systems
query _DSM on ACPI_HANDLE(dev), which is NULL on a device tree system.
ACPICA then fails with AE_BAD_PARAMETER, and acpi_evaluate_dsm() warns
about it. An Intel Wi-Fi card on a device tree board logs, for example:

  ACPI: <n/a>: failed to evaluate _DSM 2c176672-0b22-294b-814f-75e4dd26b5fd
    rev:0 func:0 (0x1001)

A device without an ACPI companion has no _DSM to evaluate. Return NULL
for it, as for a missing method, which every caller already handles.
---
 drivers/acpi/utils.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/acpi/utils.c b/drivers/acpi/utils.c
index 6ab27e4..90b2b99 100644
--- a/drivers/acpi/utils.c
+++ b/drivers/acpi/utils.c
@@ -779,6 +779,10 @@ acpi_evaluate_dsm(acpi_handle handle, const guid_t *guid, u64 rev, u64 func,
 		.pointer = params,
 	};
 
+	/* A device without an ACPI companion, as on device tree systems */
+	if (!handle)
+		return NULL;
+
 	params[0].type = ACPI_TYPE_BUFFER;
 	params[0].buffer.length = 16;
 	params[0].buffer.pointer = (u8 *)guid;
